UNPINNED  engine-src.tar (uncompressed stream of engine-src.tar.gz)
# AN ADDITIONAL, OPTIONAL PIN — and UNPINNED here is a decision taken WITH the number in hand, not
# an oversight. Read on before treating it as a gap.
#
# WHAT IT WOULD BE: the sha256 of `gzip -dc /opt/inference-bench/engine-src.tar.gz`, i.e. of the
# archive's uncompressed stream, checked by tests/test.sh BEFORE it unpacks the archive. The image
# build prints exactly that number, with the tar flags that make it reproducible
# (`--sort=name --mtime=@0 --owner=0 --group=0 --numeric-owner`, fixed member prefix `engine-src/`).
#
# MEASURED on a build of this task's image, 2026-09-14:
#
#     d737f5f1966c7fa60a997e03071c12cc68533694be38f863f5d4795119a56d49
#
# It is recorded here as a fact and NOT promoted to the enforced first field, because the two
# authorities are not equally safe to fail closed on.
#
# THE CONTENT DIGEST IS THE AUTHORITY, and it is strictly stronger. tests/pristine_tree.sha256 is a
# digest of the staged tree's CONTENT: it covers the runtime-mount route as well as the archive
# route, and it catches tampering AFTER extraction, which an archive digest cannot. It is also
# re-derivable from the pinned commit with no image build -- verified on this same build, where the
# archive's python/ subtree digests to exactly the number that file carries, over 3524 files.
#
# WHAT PINNING THIS ONE WOULD RISK, which is the whole argument. This digest is a property of the
# TAR STREAM, so it depends on the tar implementation that wrote it, not only on the content: a
# builder whose tar emits different pax headers produces a different number for a byte-identical
# tree. test.sh fails closed on a mismatch, so a builder difference would turn every scored run
# into an infrastructure zero with nothing able to clear it -- while the content digest, which cannot
# move for that reason, would have been green. A second authority that can only ever add false
# negatives is not worth enforcing.
#
# So test.sh enforces this file WHEN IT CARRIES A DIGEST and logs a skip when it says UNPINNED. If
# the build environment is ever fixed to one tar, promote the number above into the first field.
